<title>UK: UK clears Natl Express,Great West rail buys.</title>
<headline>UK clears Natl Express,Great West rail buys.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Department of Trade and Industry on Wednesday gave the green light to two railway acquisitions.</p>
<p>The DTI said it would not refer National Express Group Plc's acquisition of North London Railways Ltd and Great Western Holdings Ltd's buy of North West Regional Railways Ltd to the Monopolies and Mergers Commission.  </p>
<p>Great Western is about 51 percent owned by staff, with the remaining stake split between venture capital group 3i Group Plc and FirstBus Plc. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
</text>
